  "source": "YASKAWA AC Drive CR700 for Cranes Technical Manual, SIEPC71061723B, section 5.3 and chapter 10",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "YASKAWA AC Drive CR700 for Cranes Technical Manual",
      "version": "SIEPC71061723B",
      "url": "https://www.yaskawa.eu.com/Global%20Assets/Downloads/Technical_Documentation/Inverter_Drives/CR700/TM_SIEP-C710617-23.pdf",
      "note": "section 5.3 (tables 5.12 to 5.17) and the parameter list (b1, C1, d1, E1, E2, H5, o1, U1-U4); checked against the map attached to issue #70"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "MEMOBUS/Modbus RTU: 8 data bits and 1 stop bit (fixed). Factory defaults are node address 0x1F (31), 9600 bps (H5-02 = 3) and no parity (H5-03 = 0); after changing them, power cycle or set H5-20 = 1.",
    "Function 03 reads at most 16 registers per message; 06/10 write. Command data (0x0001-0x000F) and monitor data (0x0020-0x00FB) need no Enter command.",
    "To run from Modbus set b1-01 = 2 and b1-02 = 2. With H5-11 = 0 (default) a parameter write takes effect only after the Enter command: write 0 to 0x0900 (saved to EEPROM) or 0x0910 (RAM only).",
    "Frequency registers are scaled for o1-03 = 0 (0.01 Hz). Some current and power registers change resolution with the drive model; their scale is left at 1.",
    "Only the main parameters are listed. Every parameter has its MEMOBUS address in the manual's parameter list (chapter 10): read it with function 03 and write it as above.",
    "Do not use Modbus writes as a safety function on a crane: brake control, limits and emergency stop must stay in the drive's hardware and safety settings.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
